-    #                              which declares `environment: production`. It says "migrations
-    #                              ran", roughly 25 seconds after the merge. It says nothing at
-    #                              all about Vercel.
-    #   vercel[bot]              - "Deployment has completed". This is the deployment, and by the
-    #                              time it arrives the production alias is already promoted.
-    #
-    # Verifying on the first one is verifying minutes before production has anything new to serve,
-    # so the check could only ever pass by outrunning the deployment. Measured over the 21 landings
-    # of 2026-09-07/08 (17 of them deploy-affecting): the two statuses are 80-192 s apart, median
-    # 182 s. 14 of those 17 runs polled their whole 120 s window and went red on a production that
-    # was healthy - issue #159 and the 13 before it. The three that passed did not verify anything
-    # the others did not: two caught the alias at 56 s and 72 s on the day's two fastest builds,
-    # and one only because the runner took 150 s to start. Every run raised by the vercel[bot]
